language": {"code": "yi", "name": "Yiddish"}, "word": "סושי"}], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(countable, rare) One of the portions from this dish.", "tags": ["countable", "rare", "usually"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "You will recall that, contrary to the relative appearance of the words, the sashimi are the simple raw fish slices and the sushi are the rolls of rice and raw fish.", "reference": "1983 May 31, Robert Nadeau, “Restaurant: Gyuhama of Japan: Suit yourself with sushi”, in Richard M. Gaines, editor, The Boston Phoenix, volume XII, number 22, Boston, Mass.: Boston Phoenix Inc., →ISSN, →OCLC, section 2, page 10, column 3:"}, {"text": "Rusty put a sushi in her palm. / Mary Kate popped it into her mouth. It tasted salty and crunchy. “Cucumber!” she said. / “My grandmother puts a surprise in the middle of each one,” said Rusty.", "reference": "1989, Jean Marzollo, chapter 5, in The Green Ghost of Appleville (39 Kids on the Block; 1), New York, N.Y.: Scholastic Inc., →ISBN, page 42:"}, {"text": "I reach out and pop a sushi into my mouth while I’m waiting for someone to answer a question.", "reference": "1997, Jeffrey A. Kottler, “Focusing on People”, in Travel That Can Change Your Life: How to Create a Transformative Experience (Jossey-Bass Psychology Series), San Francisco, Calif.: Jossey-Bass Publishers, →ISBN, page 92:"}, {"text": "Startled by the venom, Erik almost dropped a sushi into his mixture of soy sauce and wasabi.", "reference": "2009 September 14, Frank Penater, “Undercover”, in The Gene Card, Bloomington, Ind.: iUniverse, →ISBN, page 161:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [], "subsenses": []}, {"definition": "(proscribed) Raw fish, especially as a Japanese dish.", "tags": ["proscribed", "uncountable", "usually"], "examples": [], "quotes": [{"text": "'Can't eat sushi?' I said. Then Mom said, 'You can't eat uncooked fish when you're pregnant' as if I'm the one stupid enough to go and get pregnant!", "reference": "2012, Alison Acheson, Molly's Cue, page 26:"}], "synonyms": [], "antonyms": [], "translations": [{"language": {"code": "sq", "name": "Albanian"}, "word": "sushi"}, {"language": {"code": "am", "name": "Amharic"}, "word": "ሱሺ"}, {"language": {"code": "ar", "name": "Arabic"}, "word": "سُوشِي"}, {"language": {"code": "hy", "name": "Armenian"}, "word": "սուշի"}, {"language": {"code": "az", "name": "Azerbaijani"}, "word": "suşi"}, {"language": {"code": "eu", "name": "Basque"}, "word": "sushi"}, {"language": {"code": "be", "name": "Belarusian"}, "word": "су́шы"}, {"language": {"code": "bn", "name": "Bengali"}, "word": "সুশি"}, {"language": {"code": "br", "name": "Breton"}, "word": "sushi"}, {"language": {"code": "bg", "name": "Bulgarian"}, "word": "су́ши"}, {"language": {"code": "my", "name": "Burmese"}, "word": "ဆူရှီ"}, {"language": {"code": "ca", "name": "Catalan"}, "word": "sushi"}, {"language": {"code": "yue", "name": "Chinese Cantonese"}, "word": "壽司 /寿司"}, {"language": {"code": "hak", "name": "Hakka Chinese"}, "word": "壽司 /寿司"}, {"language": {"code": "nan-hbl", "name": "Chinese"}, "word": "壽司 /寿司"}, {"language": {"code": "nan-hbl", "name": "Chinese"}, "word": "醋飯箍 /醋饭箍"}, {"language": {"code": "nan-hbl", "name": "Chinese"}, "word": "臭酸飯 /臭酸饭"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "壽司 /寿司"}, {"language": {"code": "cmn", "name": "Chinese Mandarin"}, "word": "日本壽司 /日本寿司"}, {"language": {"code": "cs", "name": "Czech"}, "word": "suši"}, {"language": {"code": "da", "name": "Danish"}, "word": "sushi"}, {"language": {"code": "nl", "name": "Dutch"}, "word": "sushi"}, {"language": {"code": "eo", "name": "Esperanto"}, "word": "suŝio"}, {"language": {"code": "et", "name": "Estonian"}, "word": "suši"}, {"language": {"code": "fo", "name": "Faroese"}, "word": "sushi"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "sushi"}, {"language": {"code": "fi", "name": "Finnish"}, "word": "suši"}, {"language": {"code": "fr", "name": "French"}, "word": "su